<metadata><name>Waldo Lake</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:293-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.604332" lon="-122.045626"><ele>1524.3</ele><name>Gold Lake Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin (OSM way 153751552 Gold Lake Sno-Park); confidence: high; pdf_page: 296; quote: Starting at Gold Lake Sno-Park</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.605964" lon="-122.048016"><ele>1529.8</ele><name>Gold Lake Road at the sno-park</name><desc>source: OSM node 2934688911, south end of Gold Lake Road (NF 500), at the west end of the sno-park lot; confidence: high; pdf_page: 296</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.611119" lon="-122.052594"><ele>1546.0</ele><name>Marilyn Lakes path leaves Gold Lake Road</name><desc>source: OSM node 39996097, where an unnamed path (way 563799689) leaves Gold Lake Road 0.45 mi from the sno-park and runs north between the Marilyn Lakes to Marilyn Lakes Trail #3689; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 296; quote: map 68 draws the route past Upper Marilyn Lake (4879')</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.629750" lon="-122.049780"><ele>1471.9</ele><name>Gold Lake (end of Gold Lake Road)</name><desc>source: OSM node 5351877752, north end of Gold Lake Road (NF 500) at the campground; confidence: high; pdf_page: 296; book_elev_ft: 4807; quote: the route proceeds to Gold Lake</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.631482" lon="-122.050885"><ele>1469.6</ele><name>Gold Lake Trail start</name><desc>source: OSM node 5351878089, south end of Gold Lake Trail #3677; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 296</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.633910" lon="-122.050393"><ele>1503.8</ele><name>Waldo Lake road at the Fuji Mountain trailhead</name><desc>source: OSM node 5261405477, Fuji Mountain Trail #3674 meets Waldo Road (NF 5897); 3.45 mi by road from the Betty Lake trailhead; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 296; quote: then along a tie trail to the Waldo Lake road (a snowmobile route)</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.671887" lon="-122.019694"><ele>1688.7</ele><name>Betty Lake Trailhead</name><desc>source: OSM node 2934527829, Betty Lake Trail meets Waldo Road; confidence: high; pdf_page: 296; quote: that you follow 3.6 miles to the marked Betty Lake-Waldo Lake Trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.692267" lon="-122.035850"><ele>1670.3</ele><name>Waldo Lake shore (Trail 3590)</name><desc>source: OSM node 286790097, Betty Lake Trail meets Jim Weaver Loop Trail #3590; confidence: high; pdf_page: 296; quote: From the Waldo Lake road it is 2.5 miles to the lakeshore ... descends to Waldo Lake Trail No. 3590</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.678588" lon="-122.056820"><ele>1658.9</ele><name>South Waldo Trail junction</name><desc>source: OSM node 286790179, South Waldo Trail #3586 meets Trail #3590; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 296</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.678518" lon="-122.055863"><ele>1660.6</ele><name>South Waldo Shelter</name><desc>source: OSM node 7838498751 South Waldo Shelter; confidence: high; pdf_page: 296; quote: the shelter at the south edge of South Waldo Meadows ... 300 yards from the lake</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Waldo Lake</name><desc>1. Gold Lake Sno-Park -&gt; Gold Lake Road at the sno-park: straight (high), 0.16 mi | 2. Gold Lake Road at the sno-park -&gt; Marilyn Lakes path leaves Gold Lake Road: osm (high), 0.45 mi | 3. Marilyn Lakes path leaves Gold Lake Road -&gt; Gold Lake (end of Gold Lake Road): osm (medium), 1.84 mi | 4. Gold Lake (end of Gold Lake Road) -&gt; Gold Lake Trail start: straight (medium), 0.13 mi | 5. Gold Lake Trail start -&gt; Waldo Lake road at the Fuji Mountain trailhead: osm (medium), 0.34 mi | 6. Waldo Lake road at the Fuji Mountain trailhead -&gt; Betty Lake Trailhead: osm (high), 3.45 mi | 7. Betty Lake Trailhead -&gt; Waldo Lake shore (Trail 3590): osm (high), 1.83 mi | 8. Waldo Lake shore (Trail 3590) -&gt; South Waldo Trail junction: osm (high), 1.55 mi | 9. South Waldo Trail junction -&gt; South Waldo Shelter: straight (high), 0.05 mi</desc>
